      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "I hit a crash while creating a new wallet in Bitcoin-Qt 31.1 on an Apple silicon Mac with `nosettings=1`. After looking through the crash report and code, I traced it to saving the wallet's load-on-startup setting: the settings writer throws when dynamic settings are disabled.\r\n\r\nThis checks whether settings are enabled before writing, so the wallet operation can finish with the existing warning instead of throwing.\r\n\r\nThe first commit adds unit and functional tests for the current behavior. The second adds the fix and updates those assertions.\r\n\r\nTested the focused wallet/settings unit tests, `wallet_startup.py`, `feature_settings.py`, and the Qt test suite on macOS ARM64.",
